#!/bin/bash
java -jar bx-agent/target/bx-agent-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar \
  -s examples/ast2dag/ExpressionAST.ecore \
  -t examples/ast2dag/ExpressionDAG.ecore \
  -o generated \
  -d "Transform an expression AST (ExpressionAST) to an expression DAG (ExpressionDAG). The AST is a tree where equal subexpressions may occur multiple times; the DAG collapses them into shared nodes. Source package: 'ast'. Target package: 'dag'. Both have an abstract supertype Expression with concrete subtypes Operator (has 'op: ArithmeticOperator' and containment refs 'left'/'right' to Expression), Variable (has 'name: EString'), and Number (has 'value: EInt'). The source Model has a single root expression via 'expr' (single containment). The target Model has a flat list 'exprs' of all unique Expression nodes (containment), while Operator.left and Operator.right are cross-references (not containment) in the DAG. Use a structuralDeduplicationMapping with abstractSourceType=Expression, abstractTargetType=Expression, concreteTypes=[{Operator, keyAttributes=[op], childRefs=[left,right]}, {Variable, keyAttributes=[name], childRefs=[]}, {Number, keyAttributes=[value], childRefs=[]}], sourceContainerType=Model, sourceContainerRef=expr (single, not many), targetContainerType=Model, targetContainerRef=exprs. Include Model in typeMappings (1:1). Do NOT include Expression, Operator, Variable, or Number in typeMappings, attributeMappings, or referenceMappings — the structuralDeduplicationMapping handles them. Do NOT include 'exprs', 'left', 'right', 'expr' in referenceMappings. The backward direction: given the DAG, find the root node (not referenced as a child by any other node), then recursively clone the DAG tree into an AST containment tree — shared DAG nodes produce multiple AST copies."
